                    <figure class="guide-figure"><img src="/screenshots/guides/remote-server-monitoring-01-hosts.webp" data-zoomable alt="The Hosts page with the fleet summary above a table of eight servers: each host's OS and architecture, CPU, memory and disk usage bars, 15-minute load and last-seen time, with web-04 marked Ended." width="2340" height="1490" loading="lazy" /></figure>
                    <p>
                        Click a host for CPU, memory, filesystem per mount, network per interface and load over time, next to its <code>os.type</code> and <code>host.arch</code>. Add the <code>ec2</code>, <code>gcp</code> or <code>azure</code> detector to <code>resource_detection</code> and the page also shows <code>cloud.provider</code> and <code>cloud.region</code>.
                    </p>
                    <figure class="guide-figure"><img src="/screenshots/guides/remote-server-monitoring-02-host-detail.webp" data-zoomable alt="The detail page of host db-01, marked Active: CPU, memory, disk and 15-minute load figures, the CPU and memory charts, and the host's os.type linux and host.arch amd64." width="2340" height="1576" loading="lazy" /></figure>
                    <p>
                        The system logs are on the <a href="/docs/explore/logs">Logs</a> page under the service <code>system-logs</code>. For Windows servers, the <a href="/guides/windows-server-monitoring">Windows server monitoring guide</a> sets up the same Collector.
                    </p>

                    <div class="guide-maple">
                        <p class="guide-kicker">Set it up in Maple</p>
                        <h3>Send host metrics</h3>
                        <p>The Hosts docs list each metric the page reads and the fixes for a missing host or zero readings.</p>
                        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                            <a href="/docs/infrastructure/hosts" class="guide-button guide-button--primary">Hosts docs</a>
                            <a href="/docs/alerting/alert-rules" class="guide-button">Alert rules</a>
                        </div>
