                <section id="alerts" class="scroll-mt-24">
                    <p class="guide-eyebrow"><span>06</span> · Alerts</p>
                    <h2>Alert when a remote server goes down or quiet</h2>
                    <p>
                        A Maple <a href="/docs/alerting/alert-rules">alert rule</a> checks a value every minute and opens an incident after two breaching checks in a row. A server that stops sending leaves empty windows, which rules skip unless <strong>Alert when there is no data</strong> is on. That switch doesn't apply to rules split into one incident per group, so the heartbeat gets its own rule.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The rules below use the <strong>SQL</strong> signal on the <code>metrics_gauge</code> table (<a href="/docs/reference/sql">SQL reference</a>). Open <strong>Alerts</strong>, click <strong>New rule</strong>, choose <strong>Start blank</strong>, and set the signal to <strong>SQL</strong>.
                    </p>

                    <h3 id="heartbeat" class="scroll-mt-24">Heartbeat rule per server</h3>
                    <pre><code set:html={highlight(heartbeatSql, "sql")} /></pre>
                    <ol class="guide-steps">
                        <li><span>01</span><div><h4>Threshold</h4><p><strong>Reduce each window by</strong> Sum, <strong>Alert when the value</strong> is below, <strong>Threshold</strong> <code>1</code>.</p></div></li>
                        <li><span>02</span><div><h4>How it is checked</h4><p><strong>Window</strong> 5 min and <strong>Minimum samples</strong> 1. The default of 50 would skip every check.</p></div></li>
                        <li><span>03</span><div><h4>No data</h4><p>Switch <strong>Alert when there is no data</strong> on, so a quiet <code>web-01</code> counts as a breach.</p>
                            <figure class="guide-figure"><img src="/screenshots/guides/remote-server-monitoring-03-heartbeat-rule.webp" data-zoomable alt="The alert rule form with the SQL signal and the heartbeat query for web-01, Reduce each window by Sum, is below 1, a 5 minute window, Minimum samples 1 and Alert when there is no data switched on." width="2330" height="2227" loading="lazy" /></figure></div></li>
                    </ol>
                    <p>
                        The incident opens six to seven minutes after the server's last report. Create one rule per server from your config management with the <a href="/docs/alerting/alert-rules#create-a-rule-over-the-api">alert rules API</a>.
                    </p>

                    <h3 id="fleet-heartbeat" class="scroll-mt-24">One rule for the whole fleet</h3>
                    <p>
                        Count the hosts that reported instead, and fire when the count drops below the fleet size:
                    </p>
                    <pre><code set:html={highlight(fleetSql, "sql")} /></pre>
                    <p>
                        Set <strong>Reduce each window by</strong> Minimum, <strong>Alert when the value</strong> is below, <strong>Threshold</strong> the number of servers, <strong>Minimum samples</strong> 1, and <strong>Alert when there is no data</strong> on. The Hosts page filtered to <strong>Ended</strong> shows which server went quiet. Raise the threshold when you add a server.
                    </p>

                    <h3 id="thresholds" class="scroll-mt-24">Disk, memory and CPU per host</h3>
                    <p>
                        Threshold rules don't need the no-data switch, so one rule covers every server. Return a <code>group</code> column and Maple opens one incident per host. Set <strong>Reduce each window by</strong> Maximum and <strong>Minimum samples</strong> 1; utilization is a ratio from 0 to 1.
                    </p>
                    <LanguageTabs tabs={thresholdRules.map(({ id, label }) => ({ id, label }))} label="Rule" group="maple-guide-remote-rule">
                        {thresholdRules.map((r) => (
                            <LanguageTab id={r.id}>
                                <pre><code set:html={highlight(r.sql, "sql")} /></pre>
                                <p class="tab-note" set:html={r.settings} />
                            </LanguageTab>
                        ))}
                    </LanguageTabs>
                    <p>
                        Click <strong>Test rule</strong> before you save: the preview replays the rule over a past range and shades the periods where it would have fired. <a href="/docs/alerting/incidents">Incidents</a> covers what happens next, from notifications to resolution.
                    </p>
                </section>

